Starknet privacy SDK (@starkware-libs/starknet-privacy-sdk 0.14.4-rc.2)

Source: https://github.com/starkware-libs/starknet-privacy, directory sdk/
Tag: PRIVACY-0.14.4-RC.2, commit f7fb72a9a7d0cb1a2ad447fec55c1207029ae093
License: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE in this folder, copied from the repository root)

Why it is vendored: the SDK is published only to GitHub Packages, which needs a
token to install, and has no public npm release yet. This tarball is the
package built from the tag above (npm ci, npm run build, npm pack in sdk/).

Changes from the upstream package, marked by the "-gloam.1" file name, all in
package.json "exports" (no code changed):
 - "./contract-discovery" points at the SDK's own
   dist/internal/contract-discovery.js. Upstream exposes ContractDiscoveryProvider
   only through "./testing", which also loads the devnet harness (node:fs,
   node:child_process) and so can't be bundled for the browser.
 - each entry with an "import" condition also gets "default" (the same file), so
   the app's TypeScript scripts, which tsx loads as CommonJS, resolve it too.

Replace this with the published package once StarkWare releases it on npm.
